# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Secrets — never commit real keys; .env.example is the committed template
.env

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Downloaded data (FEC bulk archives, legislators YAML, etc.)
data/raw/

# Review exchange files (promise exports / triage verdicts): working files.
# The directory is excluded by contents rather than by name, because two
# things in it are not working files. The gold set is the hand-labelled
# evidence behind every precision number we publish, and the taxonomy is the
# reasoning that produced the gate's rules. A quality claim nobody can
# reproduce is a quality claim nobody should believe, and the methodology
# page says these live in this repository, so they have to.
data/review/*
!data/review/gold_v2.jsonl
!data/review/failure_taxonomy.md

# Exported assistant session transcripts: working artifacts, never source.
/20??-??-??-*.txt

# Built snapshots: regenerated from Postgres, never source.
dist/

# Map reference geometry is derived, not authored, but it is tracked because
# the page cannot build without it and rebuilding needs tools (mapshaper) that
# are not part of the Python toolchain.
#
# us_places.json is reproducible: uv run python -m pipeline.etl.places, which
# records its source URLs and their sha256 inside the file it writes.
#
# us_cd119.topo.json is NOT currently reproducible from anything in this repo.
# It is Census cb_2024 cd119 at 3% topology-preserving simplification,
# projected to Albers USA by mapshaper, carrying both a districts and a states
# layer. The exact invocation was never recorded, and this comment used to
# claim the command lived in web/map.js, where only that prose description
# has ever been. Verified empirically instead: the projection is mapshaper's
# `albersusa`, because points projected with it land inside the correct
# district polygons of this file, insets included. Recovering the full command
# is worth doing before the lines next change.
!data/geo/us_cd119.topo.json
!data/geo/us_places.json
